      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the hybrid idea, but that feels like a bit of a cop-out. If we're looking at it through the lens of current social justice theory, isn't it true that retributive justice is fundamentally flawed because it just reinforces existing systemic inequalities? Like, how can you argue that a punishment-based system is \"morally sound\" when it's so often used to target marginalized communities?",
