      "content": "\"The consensus among progressive frameworks suggests...\" feels like a bit of a way to avoid answering. If we're moving past the \"on the one hand/on the other hand\" stage, doesn't the moral math just favor restorative justice? If the goal of a justice system is to actually reduce harm and build a better society, isn't retributive justice objectively less efficient and less moral in its outcomes?",
